  "predicted_delta_text": "**Prediction for S11_db**: **Improves by ~3 dB**.\n\n**Rationale**:  \n- Removed floating NM2 and PM2 by **connecting NM2 gate to n2 (input node)** and PM2 gate to n3 (bias node).  \n- NM2 now acts as a **source follower** from n2 to VSS, providing **source degeneration** at the input node.  \n- This reduces input capacitance seen from VIN1 via Miller effect and increases input impedance.  \n- PM2 acts as a **current source** pulling current from VDD through n3, helping set DC bias at the gate of PM1.  \n- This creates **better input impedance control** and improves **matching via degeneration**.  \n- The feedback path from n2 to NM2 gate improves stability and input match.  \n- Predicted **S11 improvement**: ~3 dB (from -1.59 dB to ~1.4 dB), still not meeting target but within reach.\n\n---",
